-integration#core-features","content":"Through OpenDAL integration, Curvine provides two core features for accessing external storage:","locale":"en"},"286":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/opendal-integration-32","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/opendal-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/opendal-integration#mount-feature---mounting-external-storage","content":"The `mount` feature allows mounting external storage systems into Curvine's namespace, making external storage appear as part of the Curvine filesystem.","locale":"en"},"287":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/opendal-integration-33","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/opendal-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/opendal-integration#load-feature---loading-external-data","content":"Mount an external path once, including its UFS credentials and endpoint, then\nload through the mounted Curvine path. This keeps credentials out of every\nLoad invocation and makes the source-to-target mapping unambiguous.","locale":"en"},"288":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/opendal-integration-34","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/opendal-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/opendal-integration#load-feature---loading-external-data","content":"When Transfer is enabled in the client configuration, the same `cv load`\ncommand submits an independent Transfer job. See\nTransfer Service deployment\nfor service and client configuration.","locale":"en"},"289":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/opendal-integration-35","page_id":"/docs/Architecture/opendal-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Architecture/opendal-integration#s3-compatible-storage-configuration","content":"| Parameter         | Description         | Example                   |\n| ----------------- | ------------------- | ------------------------- |\n| `s3.endpoint_url` | S3 service endpoint | `http://s3.amazonaws.com` |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"290":{"id":"/docs/Architecture/opendal-integration-36","page_id":"/docs/A