est client release accepted (empty = not enforced) |","locale":"en","table":"table-14"},"1290":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/conf-372","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/conf","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/conf#version-compatibility-policy","content":"| Field              | Default | Meaning                              |\n| ------------------ | ------- | ------------------------------------ |\n| `blocked_versions` | `[]`    | Versions rejected regardless of mode |","locale":"en","table":"table-14"},"1291":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/conf-373","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/conf","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/conf#version-compatibility-policy","content":"The protocol version range is a code-level contract, not an operator setting. Invalid mode strings and unparseable version bounds degrade to the lenient default instead of failing closed.","locale":"en"},"1292":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/conf-374","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/conf","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode/conf#version-compatibility-policy","content":"`enforce` mode requires Workers that report `component_info` on their heartbeat. Workers older than the release that introduced this field resolve to `MissingInfo` and are rejected, so keep `diagnose` until the whole Worker fleet has been upgraded.","locale":"en"},"1293":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode","type":"page","content":"Distributed Mode","breadcrumbs":["Documents","Deploy","Deploy Curvine Cluster","Distributed Mode"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/Deploy/Deploy-Curvine-Cluster/Distributed-Mode","locale":"en"},"1294":{"id":"/d