docs/Deploy/kubernetes-quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/kubernetes-quick-start#minikube","content":"The same values files and manifests work on minikube with the Docker driver. minikube's default StorageClass is also named `standard`.","locale":"en"},"1857":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/kubernetes-quick-start-41","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/kubernetes-quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/kubernetes-quick-start#minikube","content":"Then follow steps 2 to 4 unchanged. To clean up, run step 5 up to the `kind delete` command, then:","locale":"en"},"1858":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/kubernetes-quick-start-42","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/kubernetes-quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/kubernetes-quick-start#troubleshooting","content":"| Symptom                        | Check                                                                                                                                     |\n| ------------------------------ | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Master or worker pod `Pending` | `kubectl describe pod -n curvine <pod>`. Usually not enough memory in Docker, or no `standard` StorageClass (`kubectl get storageclass`). |","locale":"en","table":"table-1"},"1859":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/kubernetes-quick-start-43","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/kubernetes-quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/kubernetes-quick-start#troubleshooting","content":"| Symptom                                | Check                                                                                                                                           |\n| -------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| PVC `curvine-test-pvc` stays `Pending` | `kubectl logs -n curvine-system -l app=curvine-csi-controller -c csi-plugin`. Make sure `kubectl get pods -n curvine` shows the master running. |","locale":"en","table":"table-1"},"1860":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/kubernetes-quick-start-44","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/kubernetes-quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/Deploy/kubernetes-quick-start#troubleshooting","content":"| Symptom                               | Check                                                                                                                                                              |\n| ------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| Test pod stuck in `ContainerCreating` | `kubectl describe pod curvine-test`, then `kubectl logs -n curvine-system -l app=curvine-csi-node -c csi-plugin`. A missing `/dev/fuse` on the node shows up here. |","locale":"en","table":"table-1"},"1861":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/quick-start","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/quick-start","type":"page","content":"Quick Start","breadcrumbs":["Documents","Deploy"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/Deploy/quick-start","locale":"en"},"1862":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/quick-start-0","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/quick-start","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/Deploy/quick-start#start-from-a-release-package","content":"Start from a Release Package","locale":"en"},"1863":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/quick-start-1","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/quick-start","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/Deploy/quick-start#verify-the-cluster","content":"Verify the Cluster","locale":"en"},"1864":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/quick-start-2","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/quick-start","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/Deploy/quick-start#optional-compatibility-shell","content":"Optional Compatibility Shell","locale":"en"},"1865":{"id":"/docs/Deploy/quick-start-3","page_id":"/docs/Deploy/quick-start","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/Deploy/quick-start#web-ui",