ry by distribution. See Supported Linux Distributions.","locale":"en"},"2100":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse-13","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse#start-fuse","content":"Run from the installation directory (e.g. `build/dist` or the extracted release package):","locale":"en"},"2101":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse-14","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse#start-fuse","content":"**Default mount path**: `/curvine-fuse`","locale":"en"},"2102":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse-15","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse#start-fuse","content":"**Default config**: `conf/curvine-cluster.toml` (relative to current working directory when the process starts)","locale":"en"},"2103":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse-16","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse#start-fuse","content":"Use `bin/curvine-fuse.sh stop` to stop, or `bin/curvine-fuse.sh restart` to restart.","locale":"en"},"2104":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse-17","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse#use-the-mount-point","content":"Under the FUSE mount path you can use standard Linux file commands: `ls`, `cat`, `rm`, `mv`, `mkdir`, `du`, `cp`, etc.","locale":"en"},"2105":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse-18","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse#use-the-mount-point","content":"Example:","locale":"en"},"2106":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse-19","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/fuse#use-the-mount-point","content":"Data written here is stored in the Curvine cluster; you can also access paths that correspond to mounted UFS (un