":"| Operation    | HTTP request           |\n| ------------ | ---------------------- |\n| `HeadObject` | `HEAD /{bucket}/{key}` |","locale":"en","table":"table-1"},"2188":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-57","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#object-operations","content":"| Operation      | HTTP request             |\n| -------------- | ------------------------ |\n| `DeleteObject` | `DELETE /{bucket}/{key}` |","locale":"en","table":"table-1"},"2189":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-58","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#object-operations","content":"| Operation       | HTTP request                |\n| --------------- | --------------------------- |\n| `ListObjectsV2` | `GET /{bucket}?list-type=2` |","locale":"en","table":"table-1"},"2190":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-59","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#object-operations","content":"| Operation               | HTTP request            |\n| ----------------------- | ----------------------- |\n| `DeleteObjects` (batch) | `POST /{bucket}?delete` |","locale":"en","table":"table-1"},"2191":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-60","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#multipart-upload","content":"| Operation               | HTTP request                   |\n| ----------------------- | ------------------------------ |\n| `CreateMultipartUpload` | `POST /{bucket}/{key}?uploads` |","locale":"en","table":"table-2"},"2192":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-61","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#multipart-upload","content":"| Operation    | HTTP request                                       |\n| ------------ | -------------------------------------------------- |\n| `UploadPart` | `PUT /{bucket}/{key}?partNumber={n}&uploadId={id}` |","locale":"en","table":"table-2"},"2193":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-62","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#multipart-upload","content":"| Operation                 | HTTP request                         |\n| ------------------------- | ------------------------------------ |\n| `CompleteMultipartUpload` | `POST /{bucket}/{key}?uploadId={id}` |","locale":"en","table":"table-2"},"2194":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-63","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#multipart-upload","content":"`CopyObject` and `AbortMultipartUpload` are not implemented, and `ListObjectsV2` does not paginate. See Limitations.","locale":"en"},"2195":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-64","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#path-mapping","content":"The gateway maps S3 paths onto the Curvine namespace without an extra prefix:","locale":"en"},"2196":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-65","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#path-mapping","content":"| S3 path            | Curvine path |\n| ------------------ | ------------ |\n| Bucket `my-bucket` | `/my-bucket` |","locale":"en","table":"table-3"},"2197":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-66","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#path-mapping","content":"| S3 path                            | Curvine path                 |\n| ---------------------------------- | ---------------------------- |\n| Object `my-bucket/folder/file.txt` | `/my-bucket/folder/file.txt` |","locale":"en","table":"table-3"},"2198":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-67","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#path-mapping","content":"Buckets are regular Curvine directories, and objects are regular files. A bucket must exist before objects can be written to it, and it can also be browsed through FUSE, the CLI, or the SDK.","locale":"en"},"2199":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-68","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#1-build-the-gateway","content":"The binary is written to `target/release/curvine-s3-gateway`. Release packages do not ship it yet, so run it from the build output or copy it to the machine that will host the gateway.","locale":"en"},"2200":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-69","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#2-configure-the-cluster-connection","content":"The gateway reuses the regular Curvine cluster configuration file. Add an `[s3_gateway]` section for gateway-specific settings; the `[client]`, `[master]`, and other sections are used to connect to the cluster:","locale":"en"},"2201":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-70","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#2-configure-the-cluster-connection","content":"See Configuration for every option.","locale":"en"},"2202":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-71","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#3-create-credentials","content":"The gateway has no built-in default credentials. Generate a key pair and store it in the credential store:","locale":"en"},"2203":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-72","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#3-create-credentials","content":"Or register an existing pair (the access key must be 16–32 characters and the secret key 16–64 characters):","locale":"en"},"2204":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-73","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#3-create-credentials","content":"Both commands use the credential store selected by the configuration file. See Credential Management.","locale":"en"},"2205":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-74","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#4-start-the-gateway","content":"The default listen address is `0.0.0.0:9900`. Override it and the region on the command line:","locale":"en"},"2206":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-75","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#4-start-the-gateway","content":"`--listen` and `--region` override the configuration file only when they are set to a value other than their built-in defaults (`0.0.0.0:9900` and `us-east-1`). Use the configuration file for those two values, or pass a different value explicitly.","locale":"en"},"2207":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-76","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#command-line-arguments","content":"| Argument | Description                        | Default                    |\n| -------- | ---------------------------------- | -------------------------- |\n| `--conf` | Curvine cluster configuration file | `etc/curvine-cluster.toml` |","locale":"en","table":"table-4"},"2208":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-77","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#command-line-arguments","content":"| Argument   | Description                  | Default        |\n| ---------- | ---------------------------- | -------------- |\n| `--listen` | Listen address (`host:port`) | `0.0.0.0:9900` |","locale":"en","table":"table-4"},"2209":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-78","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#command-line-arguments","content":"| Argument   | Description          | Default     |\n| ---------- | -------------------- | ----------- |\n| `--region` | S3 region identifier | `us-east-1` |","locale":"en","table":"table-4"},"2210":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-79","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#command-line-arguments","content":"| Argument             | Description                        | Default                   |\n| -------------------- | ---------------------------------- | ------------------------- |\n| `--credentials-path` | Override the credential store path | Value from `[s3_gateway]` |","locale":"en","table":"table-4"},"2211":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-80","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#command-line-arguments","content":"| Argument | Description                                                        | Default |\n| -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ | ------- |\n| `serve`  | Optional subcommand; starting without a subcommand serves requests | —       |","locale":"en","table":"table-4"},"2212":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-81","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#command-line-arguments","content":"| Argument                                | Description                       | Default |\n| --------------------------------------- | --------------------------------- | ------- |\n| `credential add\\|generate\\|list\\|stats` | Credential management subcommands | —       |","locale":"en","table":"table-4"},"2213":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-82","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#s3_gateway-configuration","content":"| Parameter | Type   | Default          | Description             |\n| --------- | ------ | ---------------- | ----------------------- |\n| `listen`  | string | `\"0.0.0.0:9900\"` | Listen address and port |","locale":"en","table":"table-5"},"2214":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-83","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#s3_gateway-configuration","content":"| Parameter | Type   | Default       | Description          |\n| --------- | ------ | ------------- | -------------------- |\n| `region`  | string | `\"us-east-1\"` | S3 region identifier |","locale":"en","table":"table-5"},"2215":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-84","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#s3_gateway-configuration","content":"| Parameter      | Type   | Default               | Description                                                                          |\n| -------------- | ------ | --------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `put_temp_dir` | string | `\"/tmp/curvine-temp\"` | Temporary directory for PUT operations (regular and multipart) in local storage mode |","locale":"en","table":"table-5"},"2216":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-85","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#s3_gateway-configuration","content":"| Parameter                     | Type    | Default   | Description                                                         |\n| ----------------------------- | ------- | --------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `put_memory_buffer_threshold` | integer | `1048576` | Objects smaller than this (bytes) are buffered in memory during PUT |","locale":"en","table":"table-5"},"2217":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-86","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#s3_gateway-configuration","content":"| Parameter               | Type    | Default    | Description                                   |\n| ----------------------- | ------- | ---------- | --------------------------------------------- |\n| `put_max_memory_buffer` | integer | `16777216` | Maximum in-memory buffer size for PUT (bytes) |","locale":"en","table":"table-5"},"2218":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-87","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#s3_gateway-configuration","content":"| Parameter           | Type  | Default | Description                                    |\n| ------------------- | ----- | ------- | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| `get_chunk_size_mb` | float | `1.0`   | Read/write chunk size for GET responses, in MB |","locale":"en","table":"table-5"},"2219":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-88","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#s3_gateway-configuration","content":"| Parameter                 | Type    | Default | Description                                                  |\n| ------------------------- | ------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `enable_distributed_auth` | boolean | `false` | Store credentials in Curvine instead of the local filesystem |","locale":"en","table":"table-5"},"2220":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-89","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#s3_gateway-configuration","content":"| Parameter          | Type   | Default   | Description           |\n| ------------------ | ------ | --------- | --------------------- |\n| `credentials_path` | string | See below | Credential store path |","locale":"en","table":"table-5"},"2221":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-90","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#s3_gateway-configuration","content":"| Parameter                     | Type    | Default | Description                                   |\n| ----------------------------- | ------- | ------- | --------------------------------------------- |\n| `cache_refresh_interval_secs` | integer | `30`    | Credential cache refresh interval, in seconds |","locale":"en","table":"table-5"},"2222":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-91","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#s3_gateway-configuration","content":"`worker.enable_s3_gateway` (in the `[worker]` section) selects distributed multipart storage: upload parts are written under `/.s3temp` in Curvine instead of `put_temp_dir`, so any gateway instance can complete an upload. Setting it also switches the binary to the distributed credential store.","locale":"en"},"2223":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-92","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#s3_gateway-configuration","content":"**Credential store path:**","locale":"en"},"2224":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-93","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#s3_gateway-configuration","content":"Local mode (`enable_distributed_auth = false`): defaults to `~/.curvine/credentials.jsonl`","locale":"en"},"2225":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-94","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#s3_gateway-configuration","content":"Distributed mode (`enable_distributed_auth = true`): defaults to `/system/auth/credentials.jsonl`","locale":"en"},"2226":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-95","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#s3_gateway-configuration","content":"**Example configuration:**","locale":"en"},"2227":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-96","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#credential-management","content":"Credentials are stored in JSONL format, one entry per line:","locale":"en"},"2228":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-97","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#environment-variables","content":"| Variable                                    | Description |\n| ------------------------------------------- | ----------- |\n| `AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID` or `CURVINE_ACCESS_KEY` | Access key  |","locale":"en","table":"table-6"},"2229":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-98","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#environment-variables","content":"| Variable                                        | Description |\n| ----------------------------------------------- | ----------- |\n| `AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY` or `CURVINE_SECRET_KEY` | Secret key  |","locale":"en","table":"table-6"},"2230":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-99","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#environment-variables","content":"| Variable   | Description                                                               |\n| ---------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `RUST_LOG` | Log level (for example `info`, `debug`, `curvine_s3_gateway::auth=debug`) |","locale":"en","table":"table-6"},"2231":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-100","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#environment-variables","content":"The gateway imports environment credentials only when the configured credential store is empty; the imported pair is written to the local credential store. If neither a stored credential nor an environment pair is available, the gateway starts with an empty store and rejects every request.","locale":"en"},"2232":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-101","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#commands","content":"`credential list --show-secrets` and `credential generate` print secret keys to the terminal. Treat that output as sensitive and avoid shell history or shared logs.","locale":"en"},"2233":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-102","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#usage-examples","content":"The examples below use `AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID` and `AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY`. Export the pair you created in Getting Started first:","locale":"en"},"2234":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-103","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#range-requests","content":"Range responses use status `206` and include a `Content-Range` header. Signed requests are easiest to produce through an S3 SDK or the AWS CLI.","locale":"en"},"2235":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-104","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#multipart-upload-1","content":"`AbortMultipartUpload` is not routed yet, so an abandoned upload leaves its parts in the temporary storage directory. Remove them manually.","locale":"en"},"2236":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-105","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#single-instance","content":"Run the binary under your process manager (systemd, supervisor, Kubernetes). No start/stop script is shipped yet:","locale":"en"},"2237":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-106","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#multiple-instances","content":"The gateway is stateless apart from temporary multipart data and credentials, so it can run behind a load balancer:","locale":"en"},"2238":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-107","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#multiple-instances","content":"For more than one gateway instance, enable distributed multipart storage and distributed credentials so that any instance can complete an upload:","locale":"en"},"2239":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-108","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#multiple-instances","content":"Without distributed storage, upload parts stay in the local `put_temp_dir` of the instance that received them; a `CompleteMultipartUpload` routed to a different instance cannot find them. Alternatively, configure session affinity on the load balancer.","locale":"en"},"2240":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-109","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#monitoring-and-logging","content":"The gateway logs through `tracing` to stdout. Adjust the level with `RUST_LOG`:","locale":"en"},"2241":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-110","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#monitoring-and-logging","content":"Logs cover request handling, authentication failures, multipart operations, and filesystem errors. There is no metrics endpoint yet; use the `/healthz` endpoint for liveness checks.","locale":"en"},"2242":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-111","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#limitations","content":"`CopyObject` is not implemented; clients must download and re-upload.","locale":"en"},"2243":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-112","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#limitations","content":"`AbortMultipartUpload` is not implemented; abandoned uploads leave temporary parts behind.","locale":"en"},"2244":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-113","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#limitations","content":"`ListObjectsV2` returns a single page: `continuation-token` and `max-keys` are ignored, and `is-truncated` is always `false`.","locale":"en"},"2245":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-114","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#limitations","content":"Conditional request headers (`If-Match`, `If-None-Match`) are accepted but not evaluated.","locale":"en"},"2246":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-115","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#limitations","content":"When Curvine trash is enabled, `DeleteObject` and `DeleteBucket` move data into the recycle bin instead of removing it permanently.","locale":"en"},"2247":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-116","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#port-already-in-use","content":"Change the listen address in `[s3_gateway]` or pass a different `--listen` value:","locale":"en"},"2248":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-117","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#configuration-file-errors","content":"If the configuration file cannot be loaded, the gateway prints a warning and continues with defaults. Verify the path and TOML syntax:","locale":"en"},"2249":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-118","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#bucket-not-found","content":"Create the bucket before uploading (`aws s3 mb`), because the gateway does not create buckets implicitly.","locale":"en"},"2250":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway-119","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/s3-gateway#performance-tuning","content":"For large-object workloads, increase `get_chunk_size_mb` and make sure `put_temp_dir` is on fast local storage. When `worker.enable_s3_gateway = true`, multipart parts are written directly to Curvine and `put_temp_dir` is not used for them.","locale":"en"},"2251":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk","type":"page","content":"SDK Access","breadcrumbs":["Documents","User Manuals","Access"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk","locale":"en"},"2252":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk-0","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk#overview","content":"Overview","locale":"en"},"2253":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk-1","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk#rust-sdk","content":"Rust SDK","locale":"en"},"2254":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk-2","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk#java-sdk","content":"Java SDK","locale":"en"},"2255":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk-3","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk#python-sdk","content":"Python SDK","locale":"en"},"2256":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk-4","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk#common-configuration","content":"Common Configuration","locale":"en"},"2257":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk-5","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk","content":"Curvine provides multi-language SDKs so applications can access the Curvine filesystem via RPC (metadata from Master, block data from Workers) without using FUSE.","locale":"en"},"2258":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk-6","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk#overview","content":"| SDK      | Crate / Package                     | Use Case                                   |\n| -------- | ----------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------ |\n| **Rust** | `curvine-client` / `curvine-libsdk` | Native Rust applications, high performance |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"2259":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk-7","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk#overview","content":"| SDK      | Crate / Package                                                         | Use Case                                      |\n| -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------- |\n| **Java** | Hadoop-compatible FileSystem (`fs.cv://`), Java SDK from curvine-libsdk | Hadoop/Spark/Flink and other JVM applications |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"2260":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk-8","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk#overview","content":"| SDK        | Crate / Package                     | Use Case                   |\n| ---------- | ----------------------------------- | -------------------------- |\n| **Python** | Python bindings from curvine-libsdk | ML/data pipelines, scripts |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"2261":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk-9","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk#overview","content":"All SDKs require a running Curvine cluster (Master and Workers) and correct client configuration (e.g. `master_addrs` in `curvine-cluster.toml` or equivalent).","locale":"en"},"2262":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk-10","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk#rust-sdk","content":"Use the `curvine-client` crate (or the Rust API exposed by `curvine-libsdk`) to create files, read/write data, and list directories programmatically. Configuration is typically loaded from `curvine-cluster.toml` or via environment variables.","locale":"en"},"2263":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk-11","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk#rust-sdk","content":"For build and usage, see the Development Guide and the Curvine source repository (e.g. `curvine-client`, `curvine-libsdk`, and integration tests under `curvine-tests`).","locale":"en"},"2264":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk-12","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk#java-sdk","content":"**Hadoop FileSystem**: Configure `fs.cv.impl` and `fs.cv.default.master_addrs` in `core-site.xml` or `curvine-site.xml` so that `FileSystem.get(URI.create(\"curvine:///path\"), conf)` uses Curvine. See Deployment Preparation for `fs.cv.default.master_addrs`.","locale":"en"},"2265":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk-13","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk#java-sdk","content":"**Java API**: Use the Curvine Java SDK from curvine-libsdk for direct RPC access when not using the Hadoop FileSystem interface.","locale":"en"},"2266":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk-14","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk#java-sdk","content":"Compatible with Hadoop, Spark, Flink, and other JVM-based frameworks that support custom FileSystem implementations.","locale":"en"},"2267":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk-15","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk#python-sdk","content":"The Python SDK (from curvine-libsdk) provides a native API to read/write files and list directories on Curvine. Typical use cases include ML training, data preprocessing, and automation scripts.","locale":"en"},"2268":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk-16","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk#python-sdk","content":"For installation and examples, see the Curvine source repository and Development Guide.","locale":"en"},"2269":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk-17","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk#common-configuration","content":"**Master address**: Set `client.master_addrs` in the cluster config (e.g. `curvine-cluster.toml`) or pass the equivalent in each SDK (e.g. Java `fs.cv.default.master_addrs`). Format: `host1:8995,host2:8995`.","locale":"en"},"2270":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk-18","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk#common-configuration","content":"**Config file**: Most SDKs accept a config file path (e.g. `conf/curvine-cluster.toml`). The same file is used by the CLI (`cv`) and FUSE.","locale":"en"},"2271":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk-19","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Access/sdk#common-configuration","content":"For UFS (unified file system) access, mount UFS paths with `cv mount`; then SDK operations on the corresponding Curvine paths will follow the same semantics as Data Orchestration.","locale":"en"},"2272":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Deployment","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Deployment","type":"page","content":"Dynamic PVC In Deployment","breadcrumbs":["Documents","User Manuals","K8S CSI Driver"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Deployment","locale":"en"},"2273":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Deployment-0","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Deployment","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Deployment#example-topology","content":"Example Topology","locale":"en"},"2274":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Deployment-1","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Deployment","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Deployment#storageclass-parameters","content":"StorageClass Parameters","locale":"en"},"2275":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Deployment-2","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Deployment","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Deployment#apply-the-example","content":"Apply The Example","locale":"en"},"2276":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Deployment-3","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Deployment","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Deployment#what-the-example-creates","content":"What The Example Creates","locale":"en"},"2277":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Deployment-4","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Deployment","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Deployment#shared-pvc","content":"Shared PVC","locale":"en"},"2278":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Deployment-5","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Deployment","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Deployment#deployment","content":"Deployment","locale":"en"},"2279":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Deployment-6","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Deployment","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Deployment#verify-shared-access","content":"Verify Shared Access","locale":"en"},"2280":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Deployment-7","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Deployment","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Deployment#how-dynamic-paths-are-built","content":"How Dynamic Paths Are Built","locale":"en"},"2281":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Deployment-8","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Deployment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Deployment","content":"The current workflow uses the example manifests under `curvine-csi/examples` in the Curvine source tree:","locale":"en"},"2282":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Deployment-9","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Deployment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Deployment","content":"`storage-class.yaml`","locale":"en"},"2283":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Deployment-10","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Deployment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Deployment","content":"`pvc-curvine.yaml`","locale":"en"},"2284":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Deployment-11","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Deployment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Deployment","content":"`deployment-curvine.yaml`","locale":"en"},"2285":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Deployment-12","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Deployment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Deployment","content":"This path is for stateless workloads that want multiple replicas to share one Curvine-backed PVC.","locale":"en"},"2286":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Deployment-13","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Deployment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Deployment#example-topology","content":"`StorageClass`: `curvine-sc`","locale":"en"},"2287":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Deployment-14","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Deployment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Deployment#example-topology","content":"`PVC`: `curvine-shared-pvc`","locale":"en"},"2288":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Deployment-15","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Deployment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Deployment#example-topology","content":"`Namespace`: `curvine`","locale":"en"},"2289":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Deployment-16","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Deployment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Deployment#example-topology","content":"`Deployment`: `curvine-test-deployment`","locale":"en"},"2290":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Deployment-17","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Deployment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Deployment#example-topology","content":"`Replicas`: `3`","locale":"en"},"2291":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Deployment-18","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Deployment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs