I-Driver/Framework#static-pvs","content":"Static PVs do not need the structured dynamic `volumeHandle`. When `fs-path` is omitted, the node code falls back to `/` before generating the mount key. That means static PV reuse is effectively keyed by `master-addrs + /` unless you add an explicit `fs-path` attribute yourself.","locale":"en"},"2373":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Framework-56","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Framework","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Framework#static-pvs","content":"This behavior is inferred from the current `node.go` implementation, where missing `fs-path` is replaced with `/` before `mount-key` generation.","locale":"en"},"2374":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Framework-57","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Framework","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Framework#how-nodepublishvolume-finds-the-pod-subpath","content":"`NodePublishVolume` in `pkg/csi/node.go` computes the host subpath differently depending on the mounted root:","locale":"en"},"2375":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Framework-58","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Framework","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Framework#how-nodepublishvolume-finds-the-pod-subpath","content":"If `fs-path == /`, the host subpath is `mnt-path + curvine-path`","locale":"en"},"2376":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Framework-59","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Framework","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Framework#how-nodepublishvolume-finds-the-pod-subpath","content":"If `fs-path != /`, the host subpath is `mnt-path + relative(curvine-path, fs-path)`","locale":"en"},"2377":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Framework-60","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Framework","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/Framework#how-nodepublishvolume-finds-the-pod-s