ce` in `volumeClaimTemplates`, which matches the common StatefulSet pattern of one writer per replica.","locale":"en"},"2527":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/StatefulSet-25","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/StatefulSet","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/StatefulSet#notes","content":"The dynamically created Curvine directory is still derived from the StorageClass `fs-path` plus the generated PV name, not from the pod ordinal directly.","locale":"en"},"2528":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/StatefulSet-26","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/StatefulSet","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver/StatefulSet#notes","content":"FUSE reuse still happens at the node level based on `master-addrs + fs-path`; the pod-level data isolation comes from the subdirectory that each PVC points to.","locale":"en"},"2529":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver","type":"page","content":"K8S CSI Driver","breadcrumbs":["Documents","User Manuals","K8S CSI Driver"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/User-Manuals/K8S-CSI-Driver","locale":"en"},"2530":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Key-Features/cache","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Key-Features/cache","type":"page","content":"Cache","breadcrumbs":["Documents","User Manuals","Key Features"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Key-Features/cache","locale":"en"},"2531":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Key-Features/cache-0","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Key-Features/cache","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Key-Features/cache#1-what-is-curvine","content":"1. What Is Curvine?","locale":"en"},"2532":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Key-Features/cache-1","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Key-Features/cache","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Key-Features/cache#2-core-features","content":"2. Core Features","locale":"en"},"2533":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Key-Features/cache-2","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Key-Feat