","tags":[],"url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/release-notes#known-incompatible-versions","content":"Known Incompatible Versions","locale":"en"},"3063":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/release-notes-2","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/release-notes","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/release-notes#version-specific-incompatibilities","content":"Version-Specific Incompatibilities","locale":"en"},"3064":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/release-notes-3","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/release-notes","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/release-notes#reporting-a-new-incompatibility","content":"Reporting a New Incompatibility","locale":"en"},"3065":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/release-notes-4","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/release-notes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/release-notes","content":"This page compiles the release notes template used for each Curvine release and\nthe list of release versions known to be incompatible with other Curvine\ncomponents. Keep this page in sync whenever a version is added to\n`master.compatibility.blocked_versions` or a new protocol version is\nintroduced.","locale":"en"},"3066":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/release-notes-5","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/release-notes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/release-notes#release-notes-template","content":"Copy the template below, fill in the version and date, and ship it with the\nrelease announcement. The **Compatibility** table must match the\nCompatibility Matrix for that version.","locale":"en"},"3067":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/release-notes-6","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/release-notes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/release-notes#known-incompatible-versions","content":"Release versions are added to this list when they have critical bugs or\nprotocol-level incompatibilities that make them unsafe in a mixed-version\ncluster. The corresponding `blocked_versions` entry in the master\n`compatibility` section is the operational enforcement of these entries:\nblocked versions are **always rejected regardless of mode** (emergency\nbackstop).","locale":"en"},"3068":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/release-notes-7","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/release-notes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/release-notes#known-incompatible-versions","content":"| Version | Component | Reason                                           | Introduced In | Resolution                  |\n| ------- | --------- | ------------------------------------------------ | ------------- | --------------------------- |\n| 0.2.5   | worker    | Critical data corruption bug in batch-write path | 0.2.5         | Upgrade to 0.2.6+ or 0.3.0+ |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"3069":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/release-notes-8","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/release-notes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/release-notes#version-specific-incompatibilities","content":"**0.3.x legacy workers / clients with 0.4.x master.** Workers and clients\nrunning 0.3.x (or earlier) do not send structured `component_info`. The master\ndetects them as legacy peers: allowed with a warning in `diagnose` mode\n(default), rejected only in `enforce` mode. No data loss or protocol error\noccurs; the master simply cannot verify their protocol version, release\nversion, or capabilities.","locale":"en"},"3070":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/release-notes-9","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/release-notes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/release-notes#version-specific-incompatibilities","content":"**Pre-release vs release bounds.** Pre-release versions sort before the\ncorresponding release version (`0.4.0-alpha < 0.4.0`). If\n`min_worker_version = \"0.4.0\"` is configured, a pre-release worker is rejected\nbecause it sorts below the bound. To allow pre-releases, lower the minimum\nbound accordingly.","locale":"en"},"3071":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/release-notes-10","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/release-notes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/release-notes#reporting-a-new-incompatibility","content":"Open a GitHub issue with the **compatibility** label.","locale":"en"},"3072":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/release-notes-11","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/release-notes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/release-notes#reporting-a-new-incompatibility","content":"Include: master version, worker/client version, protocol version of each\ncomponent, the full compatibility error or warning, and reproduction steps.","locale":"en"},"3073":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/release-notes-12","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/release-notes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/release-notes#reporting-a-new-incompatibility","content":"The Curvine team evaluates and either adds the version to `blocked_versions`\nor documents the incompatibility on this page.","locale":"en"},"3074":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management","type":"page","content":"Version Management and Compatibility","breadcrumbs":["Documents","User Manuals","Operations"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management","locale":"en"},"3075":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management-0","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management#version-schema","content":"Version Schema","locale":"en"},"3076":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management-1","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management#protocol-version","content":"Protocol Version","locale":"en"},"3077":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management-2","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management#viewing-component-versions","content":"Viewing Component Versions","locale":"en"},"3078":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management-3","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management#worker-version-statistics","content":"Worker Version Statistics","locale":"en"},"3079":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management-4","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management#compatibility-between-components","content":"Compatibility Between Components","locale":"en"},"3080":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management-5","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management#master--worker","content":"Master ↔ Worker","locale":"en"},"3081":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management-6","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management#master--client-including-fuse--cli--csi","content":"Master ↔ Client (including FUSE / CLI / CSI)","locale":"en"},"3082":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management-7","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management#worker--client-data-plane","content":"Worker ↔ Client (data plane)","locale":"en"},"3083":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management-8","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management#enforcement-policy","content":"Enforcement Policy","locale":"en"},"3084":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management-9","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management#capabilities","content":"Capabilities","locale":"en"},"3085":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management-10","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management#observability","content":"Observability","locale":"en"},"3086":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management-11","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management#release-notes-and-known-incompatibilities","content":"Release Notes and Known Incompatibilities","locale":"en"},"3087":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management-12","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management","content":"This chapter describes how Curvine components version themselves and how to\noperate a cluster whose components may run different versions. Since 0.4.x\nevery binary emits structured version metadata, servers advertise a\ncompatibility contract, and the master evaluates peers with a lenient\n`diagnose`-by-default policy.","locale":"en"},"3088":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management-13","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management#version-schema","content":"All Curvine components use the same version schema:","locale":"en"},"3089":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management-14","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management#version-schema","content":"Examples: `0.4.0`, `0.4.0-alpha`, `0.5.0-rc.1+build.1234`","locale":"en"},"3090":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management-15","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management#version-schema","content":"Pre-release versions sort before the corresponding release version, following\nSemVer precedence: `0.4.0-alpha < 0.4.0-beta < 0.4.0`.","locale":"en"},"3091":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management-16","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management#protocol-version","content":"The **protocol version** is a monotonic integer that governs wire-level\ncompatibility between components. It is **not** the same as the release\nversion.","locale":"en"},"3092":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management-17","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management#protocol-version","content":"| Protocol Version | Curvine Release | Notes                               |\n| ---------------- | --------------- | ----------------------------------- |\n| 1                | 0.4.x           | Initial structured protocol version |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"3093":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management-18","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management#protocol-version","content":"A component accepts a peer whose protocol version falls within\n`[min_protocol_version, protocol_version]` of the server.","locale":"en"},"3094":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management-19","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management#viewing-component-versions","content":"Every binary prints its structured version as JSON with `--version-json`:","locale":"en"},"3095":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management-20","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management#viewing-component-versions","content":"Example output:","locale":"en"},"3096":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management-21","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management#viewing-component-versions","content":"The fields are:","locale":"en"},"3097":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management-22","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management#viewing-component-versions","content":"`component` — component name (`master`, `worker`, `client`, `fuse`, `cli`, `csi`).","locale":"en"},"3098":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management-23","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management#viewing-component-versions","content":"`release_version` — Cargo/package version of the build.","locale":"en"},"3099":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management-24","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management#viewing-component-versions","content":"`git_commit` / `git_tag` / `git_branch` — exact source provenance.","locale":"en"},"3100":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management-25","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management#viewing-component-versions","content":"`protocol_version` / `min_protocol_version` — wire protocol bounds.","locale":"en"},"3101":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management-26","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management#viewing-component-versions","content":"`capabilities` — feature-level negotiation tokens.","locale":"en"},"3102":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management-27","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management#worker-version-statistics","content":"The CLI can summarize the release-version distribution across all live\nworkers. This is the fastest way to see whether a cluster is running a\nhomogeneous set of versions or a mix of old and new workers:","locale":"en"},"3103":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management-28","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management#worker-version-statistics","content":"Example output:","locale":"en"},"3104":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management-29","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management#worker-version-statistics","content":"Workers that report structured `component_info` count under their\n`release_version`; older workers that only report the legacy\n`software_version` string are counted as `legacy (<version>)`. Workers with no\nusable version data at all are grouped under `legacy (no version)`.","locale":"en"},"3105":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management-30","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management#compatibility-between-components","content":"The master evaluates every worker heartbeat and client handshake against its\nown compatibility contract. The default behavior is **lenient**: without\nexplicit configuration the master records a warning and allows the request, so\nold components are never rejected just because they predate the structured\nversion protocol.","locale":"en"},"3106":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management-31","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management#master--worker","content":"| Master | Worker | Protocol | Default Behavior |\n| ------ | ------ | -------- | ---------------- |\n| 0.4.x  | 0.4.x  | 1        | ✅ Compatible     |","locale":"en","table":"table-1"},"3107":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management-32","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management#master--worker","content":"| Master | Worker                              | Protocol | Default Behavior                                     |\n| ------ | ----------------------------------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |\n| 0.4.x  | 0.3.x (legacy, no `component_info`) | n/a      | ⚠️ Warning in `diagnose`; rejected only in `enforce` |","locale":"en","table":"table-1"},"3108":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management-33","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management#master--worker","content":"| Master | Worker                 | Protocol | Default Behavior                                     |\n| ------ | ---------------------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |\n| 0.4.x  | < `min_worker_version` | n/a      | ⚠️ Warning in `diagnose`; rejected only in `enforce` |","locale":"en","table":"table-1"},"3109":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management-34","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management#master--client-including-fuse--cli--csi","content":"| Master | Client | Protocol | Default Behavior |\n| ------ | ------ | -------- | ---------------- |\n| 0.4.x  | 0.4.x  | 1        | ✅ Compatible     |","locale":"en","table":"table-2"},"3110":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management-35","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management#master--client-including-fuse--cli--csi","content":"| Master | Client         | Protocol | Default Behavior                                     |\n| ------ | -------------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |\n| 0.4.x  | 0.3.x (legacy) | n/a      | ⚠️ Warning in `diagnose`; rejected only in `enforce` |","locale":"en","table":"table-2"},"3111":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management-36","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management#worker--client-data-plane","content":"| Worker | Client | Protocol | Default Behavior |\n| ------ | ------ | -------- | ---------------- |\n| 0.4.x  | 0.4.x  | 1        | ✅ Compatible     |","locale":"en","table":"table-3"},"3112":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management-37","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management#worker--client-data-plane","content":"| Worker | Client         | Protocol | Default Behavior                                     |\n| ------ | -------------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |\n| 0.4.x  | 0.3.x (legacy) | n/a      | ⚠️ Warning in `diagnose`; rejected only in `enforce` |","locale":"en","table":"table-3"},"3113":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management-38","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management#enforcement-policy","content":"The compatibility policy is configured in the master configuration file:","locale":"en"},"3114":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management-39","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management#enforcement-policy","content":"**`mode = \"diagnose\"` (default):** incompatible peers are allowed, and the\nmaster logs a warning describing the peer, its version, and the expected\nbound. This is the safe default and never breaks an existing mixed-version\ncluster.","locale":"en"},"3115":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management-40","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management#enforcement-policy","content":"**`mode = \"enforce\"`:** incompatible peers are rejected with an explicit\nerror that includes the actual peer version and the upgrade suggestion.","locale":"en"},"3116":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management-41","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management#enforcement-policy","content":"**`blocked_versions`:** release versions listed here are **always rejected**\nregardless of the mode. This is an emergency backstop for known-bad builds\n(see the known-incompatible list on the release notes page).","locale":"en"},"3117":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management-42","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management#capabilities","content":"Beyond versions, features are negotiated through capability tokens that each\ncomponent advertises in its `ComponentVersion`. A feature is enabled only when\n**both** peers declare it, so a capability introduced in a newer release is\nsilently disabled until the whole data path upgrades.","locale":"en"},"3118":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management-43","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management#capabilities","content":"| Capability | Description                   | Introduced In |\n| ---------- | ----------------------------- | ------------- |\n| `transfer` | Data transfer between workers | 0.4.0         |","locale":"en","table":"table-4"},"3119":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management-44","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management#capabilities","content":"| Capability    | Description              | Introduced In |\n| ------------- | ------------------------ | ------------- |\n| `batch-write` | Batch write optimization | 0.4.0         |","locale":"en","table":"table-4"},"3120":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management-45","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management#capabilities","content":"| Capability      | Description                                 | Introduced In |\n| --------------- | ------------------------------------------- | ------------- |\n| `short-circuit` | Short-circuit read (client → worker direct) | 0.4.0         |","locale":"en","table":"table-4"},"3121":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management-46","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management#observability","content":"The master exposes compatibility metrics on the Prometheus endpoint\n(`http://<master>:9001/metrics`). See the Monitoring Metrics\npage for the full metric table.","locale":"en"},"3122":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management-47","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management#observability","content":"| Metric                  | Type  | Labels                 | Description                                            |\n| ----------------------- | ----- | ---------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `compat_worker_verdict` | Gauge | `worker_id`, `verdict` | 1 for the current compatibility verdict of each worker |","locale":"en","table":"table-5"},"3123":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management-48","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management#observability","content":"| Metric                  | Type  | Labels                   | Description                                            |\n| ----------------------- | ----- | ------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `compat_client_verdict` | Gauge | `client_addr`, `verdict` | 1 for the current compatibility verdict of each client |","locale":"en","table":"table-5"},"3124":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management-49","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management#observability","content":"| Metric                          | Type    | Labels                 | Description                                           |\n| ------------------------------- | ------- | ---------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------- |\n| `compat_enforce_rejected_total` | Counter | `component`, `verdict` | Total number of enforce-mode compatibility rejections |","locale":"en","table":"table-5"},"3125":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management-50","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management#observability","content":"`verdict` takes one of: `compatible`, `missing_info`, `blocked`,\n`protocol_mismatch`, `version_too_old`, `version_unknown`.","locale":"en"},"3126":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management-51","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/version-management#release-notes-and-known-incompatibilities","content":"Each release ships release notes that repeat the compatibility table for that\nspecific version. The known-incompatible list and the release notes template\nare maintained in the release notes page; keep the compatibility table there\nin sync whenever a version is added to `blocked_versions` or a new protocol\nversion is introduced.","locale":"en"},"3127":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/webui","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/webui","type":"page","content":"Web Management Interface","breadcrumbs":["Documents","User Manuals","Operations"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/webui","locale":"en"},"3128":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/webui-0","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/webui","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/webui#overview---cluster-overview","content":"Overview - Cluster Overview","locale":"en"},"3129":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/webui-1","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/webui","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/webui#cluster-status-information","content":"Cluster Status Information","locale":"en"},"3130":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/webui-2","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/webui","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/webui#worker-node-status","content":"Worker Node Status","locale":"en"},"3131":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/webui-3","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/webui","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/webui#storage-capacity-statistics","content":"Storage Capacity Statistics","locale":"en"},"3132":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/webui-4","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/webui","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/webui#file-system-statistics","content":"File System Statistics","locale":"en"},"3133":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/webui-5","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/webui","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/webui#browse---file-system-browser","content":"Browse - File System Browser","locale":"en"},"3134":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/webui-6","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/webui","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/webui#file-system-navigation","content":"File System Navigation","locale":"en"},"3135":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/webui-7","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/webui","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/webui#file-and-directory-management","content":"File and Directory Management","locale":"en"},"3136":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/webui-8","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/webui","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/webui#storage-statistics","content":"Storage Statistics","locale":"en"},"3137":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/webui-9","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/webui","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/webui#empty-directory-notification","content":"Empty Directory Notification","locale":"en"},"3138":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/webui-10","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/webui","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/webui#workers---worker-node-management","content":"Workers - Worker Node Management","locale":"en"},"3139":{"id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/webui-11","page_id":"/docs/User-Manuals/Operations/webui",