"page_id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices#10-common-pitfalls-and-troubleshooting","content":"10. Common Pitfalls and Troubleshooting","locale":"zh-cn"},"6689":{"id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices-39","page_id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices#11-security-recommendations","content":"11. Security Recommendations","locale":"zh-cn"},"6690":{"id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices-40","page_id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices#12-upgrade-and-maintenance","content":"12. Upgrade and Maintenance","locale":"zh-cn"},"6691":{"id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices-41","page_id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices","content":"This guide consolidates production-proven recommendations for deploying, configuring, and operating Curvine across common workload scenarios. Each section is self-contained — apply the practices relevant to your environment.","locale":"zh-cn"},"6692":{"id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices-42","page_id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices#11-cluster-sizing-guidelines","content":"| Role   | Minimum (Dev/Test) | Recommended (Production) | Notes                                             |\n| ------ | ------------------ | ------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------- |\n| Master | 1 node             | 3 nodes (Raft group)     | Odd number for quorum; 3-node tolerates 1 failure |","locale":"zh-cn","table":"table-0"},"6693":{"id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices-43","page_id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices#11-cluster-sizing-guidelines","content":"| Role   | Minimum (Dev/Test) | Recommended (Production) | Notes                                            |\n| ------ | ------------------ | ------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------ |\n| Worker | 1 node             | 3+ nodes                 | Scale horizontally based on cache capacity needs |","locale":"zh-cn","table":"table-0"},"6694":{"id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices-44","page_id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices#11-cluster-sizing-guidelines","content":"| Role | Minimum (Dev/Test)  | Recommended (Production) | Notes                                     |\n| ---- | ------------------- | ------------------------ | ----------------------------------------- |\n| FUSE | Co-located with app | 1 per compute node       | Deploy close to the workload for locality |","locale":"zh-cn","table":"table-0"},"6695":{"id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices-45","page_id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices#12-high-availability","content":"Always deploy **3 Master nodes** in production to form a Raft group. A single Master is a single point of failure.","locale":"zh-cn"},"6696":{"id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices-46","page_id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices#12-high-availability","content":"Set `journal_addrs` to list all Raft peers explicitly:","locale":"zh-cn"},"6697":{"id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices-47","page_id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices#12-high-availability","content":"Place Master nodes on separate physical hosts or availability zones to survive rack/zone failures.","locale":"zh-cn"},"6698":{"id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices-48","page_id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices#12-high-availability","content":"Use `snapshot_interval = \"6h\"` (default) to keep Raft log size bounded.","locale":"zh-cn"},"6699":{"id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices-49","page_id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices#13-production-configuration-checklist","content":"Set `CURVINE_MASTER_HOSTNAME`, `CURVINE_WORKER_HOSTNAME`, and `CURVINE_CLIENT_HOSTNAME` to routable addresses in multi-node environments.","locale":"zh-cn"},"6700":{"id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices-50","page_id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices#13-production-configuration-checklist","content":"Never use `localhost` for any hostname in distributed deployments.","locale":"zh-cn"},"6701":{"id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices-51","page_id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices#14-kubernetes-deployment","content":"Use the official Helm chart for K8s environments:","locale":"zh-cn"},"6702":{"id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices-52","page_id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices#14-kubernetes-deployment","content":"Use `ReadWriteMany` PVCs with the CSI driver for shared data access across pods.","locale":"zh-cn"},"6703":{"id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices-53","page_id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices#14-kubernetes-deployment","content":"For latency-sensitive workloads, prefer `embedded` mount mode; for FUSE isolation, use `standalone` mode.","locale":"zh-cn"},"6704":{"id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices-54","page_id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices#15-kernel-and-os-tuning","content":"Use **Linux kernel 5.0+** (e.g., Ubuntu 22.04, Rocky Linux 9) for optimal FUSE performance.","locale":"zh-cn"},"6705":{"id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices-55","page_id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices#15-kernel-and-os-tuning","content":"Avoid kernels below 4.15 in production — FUSE concurrency is severely limited.","locale":"zh-cn"},"6706":{"id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices-56","page_id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices#2-mount-mode-selection","content":"Choosing the right mount mode is the single most impactful decision for your workload.","locale":"zh-cn"},"6707":{"id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices-57","page_id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices#21-decision-matrix","content":"| Scenario                          | Recommended Mode | Rationale                                              |\n| --------------------------------- | ---------------- | ------------------------------------------------------ |\n| Read-heavy analytics over S3/HDFS | `cache_mode`     | UFS remains source of truth; Curvine accelerates reads |","locale":"zh-cn","table":"table-1"},"6708":{"id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices-58","page_id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices#21-decision-matrix","content":"| Scenario                                 | Recommended Mode | Rationale                                    |\n| ---------------------------------------- | ---------------- | -------------------------------------------- |\n| AI/ML training data (immutable datasets) | `cache_mode`     | Data rarely changes; cache hit ratio is high |","locale":"zh-cn","table":"table-1"},"6709":{"id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices-59","page_id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices#21-decision-matrix","content":"| Scenario                         | Recommended Mode | Rationale                                    |\n| -------------------------------- | ---------------- | -------------------------------------------- |\n| General-purpose POSIX filesystem | `fs_mode`        | Full random write, rename, file lock support |","locale":"zh-cn","table":"table-1"},"6710":{"id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices-60","page_id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices#21-decision-matrix","content":"| Scenario                       | Recommended Mode | Rationale                                |\n| ------------------------------ | ---------------- | ---------------------------------------- |\n| Database storage / log writing | `fs_mode`        | Requires in-place modification semantics |","locale":"zh-cn","table":"table-1"},"6711":{"id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices-61","page_id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices#21-decision-matrix","content":"| Scenario                            | Recommended Mode | Rationale                                  |\n| ----------------------------------- | ---------------- | ------------------------------------------ |\n| Shuffle data / intermediate results | `fs_mode`        | High write throughput with async UFS flush |","locale":"zh-cn","table":"table-1"},"6712":{"id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices-62","page_id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices#21-decision-matrix","content":"| Scenario                      | Recommended Mode | Rationale                                     |\n| ----------------------------- | ---------------- | --------------------------------------------- |\n| Multi-cloud unified namespace | `cache_mode`     | Transparent proxy over heterogeneous backends |","locale":"zh-cn","table":"table-1"},"6713":{"id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices-63","page_id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices#22-cache_mode-best-practices","content":"Enable `--read-verify-ufs true` **only** when UFS data changes frequently and staleness is unacceptable. It adds one extra UFS HEAD request per read.","locale":"zh-cn"},"6714":{"id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices-64","page_id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices#22-cache_mode-best-practices","content":"Use `bin/cv fs free -r /path` to release cache space safely without deleting UFS data.","locale":"zh-cn"},"6715":{"id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices-65","page_id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices#22-cache_mode-best-practices","content":"**Warning**: `delete` in cache_mode deletes UFS data. Use `free` for cache-only cleanup.","locale":"zh-cn"},"6716":{"id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices-66","page_id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices#23-fs_mode-best-practices","content":"Run `bin/cv mount resync /workspace` after external UFS changes to synchronize metadata.","locale":"zh-cn"},"6717":{"id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices-67","page_id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices#23-fs_mode-best-practices","content":"**Never rename large directories** on S3/OSS backends — it triggers full data copy.","locale":"zh-cn"},"6718":{"id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices-68","page_id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices#23-fs_mode-best-practices","content":"Set `--replicas 2` or higher for critical data to survive Worker failures.","locale":"zh-cn"},"6719":{"id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices-69","page_id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices#32-match-storage-tier-to-data-temperature","content":"| Data Temperature      | Storage Tier | TTL | Replicas | Example                       |\n| --------------------- | ------------ | --- | -------- | ----------------------------- |\n| Hot (frequent access) | MEM          | 1d  | 2-3      | Model weights, feature tables |","locale":"zh-cn","table":"table-2"},"6720":{"id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices-70","page_id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices#32-match-storage-tier-to-data-temperature","content":"| Data Temperature      | Storage Tier | TTL | Replicas | Example                          |\n| --------------------- | ------------ | --- | -------- | -------------------------------- |\n| Warm (regular access) | SSD          | 7d  | 2        | Training datasets, Parquet files |","locale":"zh-cn","table":"table-2"},"6721":{"id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices-71","page_id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices#32-match-storage-tier-to-data-temperature","content":"| Data Temperature         | Storage Tier | TTL | Replicas | Example                   |\n| ------------------------ | ------------ | --- | -------- | ------------------------- |\n| Cold (infrequent access) | HDD          | 30d | 1        | Archives, historical logs |","locale":"zh-cn","table":"table-2"},"6722":{"id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices-72","page_id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices#42-client-side-tuning-by-workload","content":"**Sequential read (large files > 100GB):**","locale":"zh-cn"},"6723":{"id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices-73","page_id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices#42-client-side-tuning-by-workload","content":"**High-concurrency small files (> 1000 concurrent):**","locale":"zh-cn"},"6724":{"id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices-74","page_id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices#42-client-side-tuning-by-workload","content":"**Random read:**","locale":"zh-cn"},"6725":{"id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices-75","page_id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices#43-fuse-optimization","content":"**Always use FUSE3** in production — FUSE2 delivers only ~50% of FUSE3 throughput.","locale":"zh-cn"},"6726":{"id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices-76","page_id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices#43-fuse-optimization","content":"If stuck on FUSE2, use multiple mount points:","locale":"zh-cn"},"6727":{"id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices-77","page_id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices#43-fuse-optimization","content":"For memory-constrained FUSE nodes:","locale":"zh-cn"},"6728":{"id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices-78","page_id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices#43-fuse-optimization","content":"Curvine FUSE is fully asynchronous — `attr_timeout` and `entry_timeout` are optional. Increase them for read-heavy workloads with stable metadata:","locale":"zh-cn"},"6729":{"id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices-79","page_id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices#43-fuse-optimization","content":"Set `entry_timeout = 0` and `attr_timeout = 0` if you need real-time visibility of changes from other clients.","locale":"zh-cn"},"6730":{"id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices-80","page_id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices#51-ttl-strategy","content":"| Workload                   | TTL | TTL Action | Rationale            |\n| -------------------------- | --- | ---------- | -------------------- |\n| Streaming / real-time data | 1h  | delete     | Data expires quickly |","locale":"zh-cn","table":"table-3"},"6731":{"id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices-81","page_id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices#51-ttl-strategy","content":"| Workload              | TTL     | TTL Action | Rationale                |\n| --------------------- | ------- | ---------- | ------------------------ |\n| Daily batch analytics | 1d - 7d | delete     | Aligns with job schedule |","locale":"zh-cn","table":"table-3"},"6732":{"id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices-82","page_id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices#51-ttl-strategy","content":"| Workload                | TTL      | TTL Action | Rationale                     |\n| ----------------------- | -------- | ---------- | ----------------------------- |\n| Model training datasets | 7d - 30d | free       | Keep metadata, release blocks |","locale":"zh-cn","table":"table-3"},"6733":{"id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices-83","page_id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices#51-ttl-strategy","content":"| Workload             | TTL          | TTL Action | Rationale                           |\n| -------------------- | ------------ | ---------- | ----------------------------------- |\n| Persistent workspace | 0 (disabled) | none       | Data lives until explicitly deleted |","locale":"zh-cn","table":"table-3"},"6734":{"id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices-84","page_id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices#51-ttl-strategy","content":"When using `rclone` or similar tools that preserve `mtime`, imported files may immediately expire. Verify TTL settings before large-scale imports, or temporarily disable TTL.","locale":"zh-cn"},"6735":{"id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices-85","page_id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices#52-quota-based-eviction","content":"Enable LRU eviction to prevent storage exhaustion:","locale":"zh-cn"},"6736":{"id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices-86","page_id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices#52-quota-based-eviction","content":"Files with `ttl_action = \"none\"` are **exempt** from LRU eviction — use this for critical data.","locale":"zh-cn"},"6737":{"id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices-87","page_id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices#53-data-preloading","content":"Warm up the cache before peak workloads:","locale":"zh-cn"},"6738":{"id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices-88","page_id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices#53-data-preloading","content":"Automatic caching is enabled per-mount when TTL > 0. First reads trigger background load jobs.","locale":"zh-cn"},"6739":{"id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices-89","page_id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices#53-data-preloading","content":"Combine proactive + automatic caching for best hit ratio.","locale":"zh-cn"},"6740":{"id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices-90","page_id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices#61-training-data-access","content":"Use FUSE mount point directly in PyTorch/TensorFlow data loaders — no code changes needed.","locale":"zh-cn"},"6741":{"id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices-91","page_id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices#61-training-data-access","content":"Set `num_workers=8` in DataLoader for parallel FUSE reads.","locale":"zh-cn"},"6742":{"id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices-92","page_id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices#61-training-data-access","content":"Pre-load datasets before training starts: `bin/cv load s3://datasets/imagenet -w`","locale":"zh-cn"},"6743":{"id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices-93","page_id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices#62-model-serving","content":"Use `--ttl-ms 0` (no expiration) for model files that must always be available.","locale":"zh-cn"},"6744":{"id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices-94","page_id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices#62-model-serving","content":"Enable `--read-verify-ufs` to detect model version updates pushed to UFS.","locale":"zh-cn"},"6745":{"id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices-95","page_id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices#71-spark-integration","content":"For zero-code acceleration, use the S3A transparent proxy:","locale":"zh-cn"},"6746":{"id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices-96","page_id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices#71-spark-integration","content":"Mounted paths automatically use Curvine cache; unmounted paths fall through to native S3.","locale":"zh-cn"},"6747":{"id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices-97","page_id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices#72-shuffle-acceleration","content":"Use `fs_mode` mounts for shuffle data to benefit from full write acceleration.","locale":"zh-cn"},"6748":{"id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices-98","page_id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices#72-shuffle-acceleration","content":"Set `--storage-type ssd` for shuffle — memory is too expensive for ephemeral data.","locale":"zh-cn"},"6749":{"id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices-99","page_id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices#72-shuffle-acceleration","content":"Use short TTL (`1h`-`4h`) since shuffle data is transient.","locale":"zh-cn"},"6750":{"id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices-100","page_id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices#73-block-size-selection","content":"| Data Pattern        | Recommended Block Size | Rationale                                     |\n| ------------------- | ---------------------- | --------------------------------------------- |\n| Small files (< 4MB) | 4MB                    | One block per file, minimal metadata overhead |","locale":"zh-cn","table":"table-4"},"6751":{"id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices-101","page_id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices#73-block-size-selection","content":"| Data Pattern            | Recommended Block Size | Rationale                         |\n| ----------------------- | ---------------------- | --------------------------------- |\n| Parquet / ORC analytics | 128MB (default)        | Balanced parallelism and locality |","locale":"zh-cn","table":"table-4"},"6752":{"id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices-102","page_id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices#73-block-size-selection","content":"| Data Pattern           | Recommended Block Size | Rationale                                 |\n| ---------------------- | ---------------------- | ----------------------------------------- |\n| Large sequential files | 1GB                    | Reduces connection count for random reads |","locale":"zh-cn","table":"table-4"},"6753":{"id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices-103","page_id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices#73-block-size-selection","content":"| Data Pattern           | Recommended Block Size | Rationale                         |\n| ---------------------- | ---------------------- | --------------------------------- |\n| Video / model binaries | 256MB - 1GB            | High throughput sequential access |","locale":"zh-cn","table":"table-4"},"6754":{"id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices-104","page_id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices#81-metrics-endpoints","content":"| Component | Endpoint                     | Port |\n| --------- | ---------------------------- | ---- |\n| Master    | `http://<host>:9001/metrics` | 9001 |","locale":"zh-cn","table":"table-5"},"6755":{"id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices-105","page_id":"/zh-cn/docs/User-Manuals/best-practices","tags":[],"type":"text","u